<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://schema.org/funding> <https://www.pole-valorial.fr> .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An ontology designed to define the various products of the agri-food industry and the arguments associated with them in terms of their perceived naturalness."@en .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Une ontologie conÃ§ue pour dÃ©finir les diffÃ©rents produits de l'industrie agroalimentaire et les arguments qui leur sont associÃ©s en termes de naturalitÃ© perÃ§ue."@fr .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Natcl'inn ontology"@en .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ontologie Natcl'inn"@fr .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0.0" .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/fundedBy> <https://www.pole-valorial.fr> .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <https://w3id.org/afy/vocab#introduction> "NATCLâ€™INN aims to offer a solution to agri-food companies that need to balance different product attributes related to naturalness in order to meet new consumer expectations and perceptions regarding food naturalness. In order to propose a prototype Decision Support Tool, the R&D teams at ADRIA, the LEGO laboratory at the University of Western Brittany (UBO), INRAE research units and their industrial partners (Bridor, Paticeo, Charles Christ, La PAM, Ecomiam, Fleury Michon, Guyader Gastronomie) have joined forces to carry out an ambitious collaborative R&D programme. The NATCL'INN project has been certified by the VALORIAL competitiveness cluster and has received support from the Brittany Region, the Pays de la Loire Region and Quimper Bretagne Occidentale. The project began on 1 January 2024 and will be completed at the end of 2027"@en .
<https://natclinn.github.io/NatclinnTbox> <https://w3id.org/afy/vocab#introduction> "NATCLâ€™INN vise Ã  proposer une solution aux entreprises de lâ€™agroalimentaire qui doivent rÃ©aliser des arbitrages entre diffÃ©rents attributs produits relatifs Ã  la naturalitÃ© en vue de rÃ©pondre aux nouvelles attentes et reprÃ©sentations des consommateurs en matiÃ¨re de naturalitÃ© alimentaire. Afin de proposer un prototype dâ€™Outil dâ€™Aide Ã  la DÃ©cision, les Ã©quipes de R&D de lâ€™ADRIA, le laboratoire LEGO de lâ€™UniversitÃ© de Bretagne Occidentale (UBO), les unitÃ©s de recherche INRAE et leurs partenaires industriels (Bridor, Paticeo, Charles Christ, La PAM, Ecomiam, Fleury Michon, Guyader Gastronomie) se sont associÃ©s pour mener un programme ambitieux de R&D collaborative. Le projet NATCLâ€™INN a Ã©tÃ© labellisÃ© par le pÃ´le de compÃ©titivitÃ© VALORIAL et a reÃ§u le soutien de la RÃ©gion Bretagne, de la RÃ©gion Pays de la Loire et de Quimper Bretagne Occidentale. Le projet a dÃ©marrÃ© au 1er janvier 2024 et s'achÃ¨vera fin 2027."@fr .
